UID:848d6bf9364df230629e8c7e53e985382175164e@pushpin.city
DTSTAMP:20261114T153123Z
DTSTART:20261203T230000Z
DTEND:20261204T010000Z
SUMMARY:Meriem Chabani. Communion It is embarrassing to believe. It is terr
 ifying to care. What happens when we dare anyway?
LOCATION:MIT\, 77 Massachusetts Ave\, Cambridge\, MA 02139
DESCRIPTION:Algerian born\, Paris based Meriem Chabani is the founder and P
 rincipal of NEW SOUTH\, an award-winning architecture\, urban planning and
  anthropology practice that puts the margin at the center. Her work on civ
 ic spaces\, memory and belonging includes includes the Taungdwingyi cultur
 al center in Myanmar\, the Globe Aroma refugee art center in Brussels\, an
 d the upcoming Mosque Zero in Paris. She is currently a finalist for the N
 ational Slavery Museum in Amsterdam. As an educator\, Chabani has taught a
 nd lectured extensively. She has notably served as Aga Khan Design Critic 
 in Architecture at Harvard GSD (USA)\, and currently teaches at Ecole Pari
 s Malaquais (FR). Her work has regularly been distinguished and showcased 
 at a number of international architecture Biennials\, including Venice\, I
 stanbul\, Oslo and Lagos. In 2020 Chabani won the Europe 40 under 40 award
  from The European Centre for Architecture and The Chicago Athenaeum. In 2
 023\, she is one of the emerging women architects for AMC. In 2025\, Le Mo
 nde names her one of the leading voices in culture in France.\nhttps://cal
 endar.mit.edu/event/meriem-chabani-communion-it-is-embarrassing-to-believe
 -it-is-terrifying-to-care-what-happens-when-we-dare-anyway\nFrom Pushpin B
 oston: https://pushpin.city/
URL:https://calendar.mit.edu/event/meriem-chabani-communion-it-is-embarrass
 ing-to-believe-it-is-terrifying-to-care-what-happens-when-we-dare-anyway
END:VEVENT
