BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:e8c44d9dbc357434aa5bd024c27b28cb3f372eed@pushpin.city
DTSTAMP:20261114T153123Z
DTSTART:20261210T170000Z
DTEND:20261210T190000Z
SUMMARY:Author Talk: Cotten Seiler on “White Care”
LOCATION:Boston Public Library\, 700 Boylston Street\, Boston\, MA 02116
DESCRIPTION:Join Dickinson College professor Cotten Seiler for a conversati
 on about his new book\, White Care. The book discusses how few of us\, goi
 ng about our daily lives\, notice the infrastructure that surrounds us and
  makes those lives possible. What also remains hidden in plain sight is ho
 w public infrastructure in the United States has been shaped by theories o
 f race and human evolution. Cotten Seiler’s White Care shows that\, from
  the late 1800s to the present\, expert assessments of the quality of the 
 national population have both driven and thwarted the state’s provision 
 of infrastructures of water\, sanitation\, energy\, transportation\, recre
 ation\, and education. If a nation’s infrastructure is a concrete measur
 e of its belief in its population’s future\, what does the current state
  of American infrastructure say about us?\nhttps://bpl.bibliocommons.com/e
 vents/6aea33f296ec3a003adf1244\nFrom Pushpin Boston: https://pushpin.city/
URL:https://bpl.bibliocommons.com/events/6aea33f296ec3a003adf1244
END:VEVENT
