BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:b2e47d7d5bc20521ad2c229ff4a5a64d7bce01e9@pushpin.city
DTSTAMP:20261114T153123Z
DTSTART:20261212T000000Z
DTEND:20261212T020000Z
SUMMARY:The Inevitable Return: Exploding Plastic Revisited
LOCATION:ICA\, 25 Harbor Shore Dr\, Boston\, MA 02210
DESCRIPTION:On October 29\, 1966\, the ICA/Boston hosted a groundbreaking m
 ultimedia performance by Andy Warhol and the Velvet Underground under the 
 enigmatic title “Exploding Plastic Inevitable.” Presented as part of W
 arhol’s second-ever museum exhibition\, the event invited audiences to e
 xperience a cacophony of durational light and sound activations\, meant to
  challenge any expectations of instant pleasure or gratification. The Velv
 et Underground had become well-known for their dark\, minimalist\, and occ
 asionally abrasive sound. Among Warhol’s goals for the piece were to exp
 lore the capacity to bestow renewed interest upon details that are often s
 ubmerged in the normative\, evenly lit flow of time. In addition to live m
 usic\, the night consisted of film projections\, a variety of strobe and s
 potlights\, and choreographed dance\, to create a singular\, and confronta
 tional\, total-art experience.\nhttps://www.icaboston.org/events/the-inevi
 table-return-exploding-plastic-revisited/\nFrom Pushpin Boston: https://pu
 shpin.city/
URL:https://www.icaboston.org/events/the-inevitable-return-exploding-plasti
 c-revisited/
END:VEVENT
